The two operations requests aren't included. The node's world only grants `aap:caps/response-channel`. There is no filesystem import for the log file and no `http-client` import for the metadata service. Adding either would mean widening the node's authority beyond its declared capabilities, so the body only sends the reply and returns the host's confirmation.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

